# Tools that BUILD the shipped desktop artifacts (.github/workflows/build-release.yml).
#
# requirements-lock.txt hash-locks what the app imports at runtime, but pip,
# setuptools, wheel, maturin (builds the bundled PyO3 wheel) and PyInstaller
# (freezes auralis-backend and embeds its bootloader) used to be installed
# unpinned on every tag build, so a hijacked PyPI release of any of them -- or of
# pefile, altgraph, pyinstaller-hooks-contrib -- would have been baked into all
# three installers, with SHA256SUMS generated from the already-tainted output
# (#6151).
#
# Compile (shared packages are held at the runtime lock's versions via -c):
#   uv pip compile requirements-build.in --generate-hashes --universal \
#     --python-version 3.14 -c requirements-lock.txt -o requirements-build.txt
pip
setuptools
wheel
maturin
pyinstaller
